# US-129257 — EPQ Follow-Up Tab Bulk Cleanup (One-Time Script) — Detailed Analysis

> Module: Business Tools → Exception Processing Queue → Follow-Up tab. One-time administrative
> data-fix script against `LASTax`. No application code (DAL/BLL/UI/Dispatcher) is changed —
> this script is run directly against the database, outside the Remoting/API path.

---

## 1. Overview

The Follow-Up tab (`ExcpetionQueueFollowup.aspx` → `USP_ExceptionQueue_FollowUp_Sel`) shows a task
whenever, for its latest `SeqNo` per `(ExceptionID, SystemCode)`: `tbl_ExceptionQueue_UserTracking
.isFollowUp = 1` and the matching `tbl_ExceptionQueue_FollowUp_Notes` row has `isFollowUp = 1`
and a real (non-blank) `FollowUpDate`. Over 7,500 such rows have accumulated, some since 2020.

The normal "Complete" action (`usp_ExceptionQueue_CompletedItems_Upd`, used by the loan-detail
pages) does more than close a task — depending on `SystemCode`/`PaymentStatus` it also flips
`tbl_ExceptionQueue` indicator columns (`DLQResearchInd`/`DLQMonthlyUpdatesInd`/
`TaxSaleResearchInd`) and, for DIR items with a delinquent payment status, **inserts a new
`tbl_ExceptionQueue_Tax_Info` row that pushes the item into the DMU queue**. Looping that SP for
the whole backlog risks creating new/duplicate items — exactly what this story's acceptance
criteria (#5) prohibits, and very likely how the duplicate backlog built up in the first place.

**Decision (confirmed with PO):** build a new, narrowly-scoped one-time script that only touches
`tbl_ExceptionQueue_UserTracking`, `tbl_ExceptionQueue_FollowUp_Notes`, and
`tbl_ExceptionQueue_History` — archiving before every update, matching the existing convention in
these stored procedures — and explicitly leaves `tbl_ExceptionQueue` and
`tbl_ExceptionQueue_Tax_Info` untouched.

Two sub-populations exist within "everything currently on the Follow-Up tab":
- **Genuinely open** (`isComplete` = 0/NULL): get the full completion stamp.
- **Already completed, stale flag only** (`isComplete` already = 1, `isFollowUp` never cleared):
  only the flag is cleared; original `CompletedDate`/`TaggedUser`/`UpdatedBy` are preserved.

Both sub-populations still receive the standardized note and history entry, so every task this
script touches is traceable back to this cleanup.

