## 8. Validation Rules

- The eligible population is captured once into `#EligibleFollowUp` before any write occurs, so
  every later step (archive, update, note insert, history insert) acts against a fixed, consistent
  snapshot rather than criteria that could shift as rows are updated mid-script.
- Every write statement joins back to `#EligibleFollowUp` by `UserTrackingID` (or
  `ExceptionID`/`SystemCode`/`SeqNo`) — nothing outside the identified population is touched.

---

## 9. Error Handling

The whole script runs inside a single transaction (`TRY`/`CATCH`, matching the pattern already
used in `usp_ExceptionQueue_Save_FollowUps`). Any failure on any step rolls back everything —
either all identified tasks are closed and noted, or none are. The script is not partially
applied.

