## 13. Edge Cases

| Case | Handling |
|---|---|
| A task's tracking row has `isPendingQC = 1` at run time (not observed in current data, but schema allows it) | Script clears it to 0 along with `isFollowUp`, matching the same behavior as the standard Complete action. Flagging for awareness since it's a judgment call if any such row exists in Production. |
| Multiple `tbl_ExceptionQueue_FollowUp_Notes` rows share the same `(ExceptionID, SystemCode, SeqNo)` | All matching note rows are archived and flag-cleared; only **one** new standardized closure note is inserted per task (not one per existing note row). |
| An `ExceptionID` with no matching `tbl_ExceptionQueue` row | The note/history inserts (which join to `tbl_ExceptionQueue` for Loan/Lender/Agency/Tax details) would simply skip such a row. Not expected — every eligible row was confirmed to have a matching parent record during analysis. |

